---
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { absoluteUrl, defaultSocialImage, legalPageSchema } from "../lib/site";
import "../styles/service.css";

const title = "Privacy Policy | EMC2Ops";
const description =
  "Privacy policy for EMC2Ops website visitors, workflow audit requests, newsletter subscribers, and business contacts.";
const updatedAt = "2026-07-21";
---

<SiteLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={absoluteUrl("/privacy/")}
  image={absoluteUrl(defaultSocialImage)}
  imageAlt="EMC2Ops property management automation workflow."
  schema={legalPageSchema({
    path: "/privacy/",
    title,
    description,
    pageType: "PrivacyPolicy",
    updatedAt,
  })}
  pageClass="service-page"
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main>
    <section class="service-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>Privacy
        </nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="dek">How EMC2Ops handles website, newsletter, and workflow audit information.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap detail-section">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updatedAt}</p>
      <p>
        EMC2Ops provides AI front desk and workflow automation services for property management
        companies. This policy explains what information we collect through this website and related
        business forms, how we use it, and how to contact us.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We may collect information you submit through forms, including your name, email address,
        phone number, company name, company website, portfolio size, workflow needs, preferred
        meeting time, and message details. Newsletter forms collect your email address, source page,
        and subscription status.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you use the EMC2Ops website assistant, we collect the questions and conversation context
        you choose to submit so the assistant can respond. Do not submit passwords, API keys,
        resident records, payment information, government identifiers, health information, or other
        sensitive data through the assistant.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may also collect technical information such as page URL, browser user agent, basic
        analytics events, and server logs to operate, secure, and improve the site.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to workflow audit requests and business inquiries.</li>
        <li>Answer website assistant questions and help visitors find relevant services.</li>
        <li>Send requested newsletters or content updates.</li>
        <li>Operate forms, notifications, scheduling, and website analytics.</li>
        <li>Improve EMC2Ops services, content, and website performance.</li>
        <li>Protect against spam, abuse, security issues, and unauthorized use.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>
        EMC2Ops may use third-party providers for hosting, analytics, email, database storage,
        form routing, notifications, CRM workflows, and automation infrastructure. These providers
        process information only as needed to support the website and business operations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Website assistant messages are sent to OpenAI to generate a response. The assistant endpoint
        requests that generated responses are not stored for later retrieval through the API, while
        OpenAI may still process or retain limited data under its applicable service, safety, and
        legal terms. EMC2Ops does not include assistant message text in its application logs.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletter choices</h2>
      <p>
        Newsletter emails include an unsubscribe option. You can also request removal by emailing
        <a href="mailto:soya@getemc2ops.com">soya@getemc2ops.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain business inquiry and newsletter information for as long as needed to provide
        services, maintain records, resolve issues, and meet operational or legal obligations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Website assistant conversation history may be stored in your browser session so the
        conversation can continue while you browse the site. Closing the browser tab or clearing
        site data removes that browser-session copy.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access, correction, or deletion of personal information by contacting
        <a href="mailto:soya@getemc2ops.com">soya@getemc2ops.com</a>. We may need to retain limited
        records where required for security, compliance, or legitimate business purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:soya@getemc2ops.com">soya@getemc2ops.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</SiteLayout>
